---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/notes.css';

// R128: First-time-visitor FAQ. Plain English, anonymous voice,
// no "we" / "Pulse team" / "by Roman" / marketing fluff. Links go to
// /pricing/, /download/, /license/, /privacy/. <details>/<summary>
// for collapsibles (no JS).
// R279 Luna: freemium model — Free tier (100K GPT-4o mini tokens/mo)
// is the default, Pro is $20/mo or $192/yr with unlimited everything.
// 14-day Pro trial for new signups.

const PAGE_TITLE = 'Pulse — Frequently asked questions';
const PAGE_DESC =
  'Common questions about Pulse: Free vs Pro, GPT-4o mini token cap, Pro pricing, privacy, offline use, supported platforms, and how to report issues. Plain answers, no marketing.';

// Q&A content lives in the frontmatter so the structured-data block
// (FAQPage JSON-LD) is generated from the same source of truth.
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What's the difference between Free and Pro?",
    a: 'Free uses GPT-4o mini for cloud model access with a 100,000 token monthly cap, no credit card. Pro gives unlimited tokens on every cloud model we route (GPT-4o, Claude Sonnet and Haiku, Gemini Flash) plus cloud Whisper voice input, multi-model hot-swap, and unlimited web search. Both tiers include the full local Ollama routing path with no token cap on local models. New signups get a 14-day Pro trial — the whole product with no limit — and after 14 days can downgrade to Free or stay on Pro.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the Free tier really free forever?',
    a: 'Yes. The 100K tokens per month on GPT-4o mini is the rate limit on the cloud model path. Local Ollama routing has no token cap on Free — run any model you have on your machine and Pulse routes the prompts there. The Free tier does not expire, does not require a credit card, and does not ask for an email.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens after the 14-day Pro trial?',
    a: 'After 14 days the Pro features pause: cloud Whisper, multi-model hot-swap, unlimited web search, and access to GPT-4o / Claude / Gemini all stop. Free tier features keep working exactly as before. You can subscribe to Pro any time from the in-app account screen — the license key arrives by email and unlocks Pro for the billing period you picked.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much does Pro cost?',
    a: 'Pro is $20 per month, or $192 per year (save $48 vs monthly). Billing is in crypto via NOWPayments (BTC, USDT-TRC20, XMR) because the team is based in Belarus and Stripe, Polar.sh, Paddle, Lemon Squeezy, and Gumroad do not pay out to Belarusian bank accounts. There is no lifetime deal and no student discount. The 14-day Pro trial is the only way to try Pro before paying.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is the 100K GPT-4o mini cap counted?',
    a: 'Tokens in plus tokens out, across all cloud model prompts in a calendar month. A typical Q&A is around 500-1,500 tokens end-to-end, so 100K covers roughly 70-200 exchanges per month for everyday use. Local Ollama prompts do not count against the cap. The cap resets on the first of each month in your local timezone. You can see your running total in Settings → Usage.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I receive my Pro license key after I pay?',
    a: 'After the NOWPayments webhook confirms your transaction, a Cloudflare Email Service worker sends the 24-character license key to the email address you entered at checkout. The key is also written to your account at <code>ownlocalml.com/account/</code> and is recoverable any time from the receipt email. If the email does not arrive within 10 minutes, write to the support address on the receipt and we resend.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need to sign up for an account to use Free?',
    a: 'No. Pulse does not require an account, email, phone number, or sign-in to use the Free tier. Download the installer, run it, open the app. Pro needs a license key, which is delivered by email after checkout, but the app itself does not log you in to use Free.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is my data private?',
    a: 'Yes. Notes, chats, voice transcriptions, and routing mode caches never leave your device. The cloud model calls (GPT-4o mini on Free, GPT-4o / Claude / Gemini on Pro) are sent directly to the provider under your prompts. Pulse does not run an analytics SDK, an error reporter, or a "phone home" endpoint. You can verify the network calls in the app logs (Settings → Logs). The full data model is on the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use Pulse offline?',
    a: 'Yes for local models. If Pulse talks to an Ollama model on your machine and the model is already pulled, the full prompt-response cycle works offline: hotkey opens the panel, prompt goes to Ollama over <code>localhost</code>, response streams back. Internet is only required for cloud model calls (GPT-4o mini, GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini), the optional update check, and any Smart Engine tool that hits the network (HN, RSS).',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use my own AI model?',
    a: 'Yes. Pulse for Windows talks to any OpenAI-compatible local endpoint. Ollama works out of the box (run <code>ollama serve</code> and Pulse finds it). LM Studio, vLLM, llama.cpp, and any other server that speaks the OpenAI HTTP API also work. Pulse does not lock you to a provider or a model, and local Ollama routing has no token cap on either Free or Pro.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you offer refunds?',
    a: 'Yes — 30-day money-back on any Pro purchase, no questions asked. Email the support address from your receipt and the refund goes through the same NOWPayments channel you paid with. After 30 days, Pro is still cancelable at any time but is not refunded for the unused billing period.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is payment crypto-only?',
    a: 'The Pulse team is based in Brest, Belarus, and Stripe, Polar.sh, Paddle, Lemon Squeezy, and Gumroad do not pay out to Belarusian bank accounts. NOWPayments handles BTC, USDT-TRC20, and XMR at 0.5% per transaction and pays out in the same currencies. The only fiat-shaped piece is the Cloudflare Email Service worker that sends the license key after the NOWPayments webhook fires. If you need an invoice in USD or EUR, write to the support email and we can do a manual stablecoin transfer.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which platforms are supported?',
    a: 'Windows 10 and 11 (NSIS or MSI installer) and Android 7.0+ (sideloaded APK). iOS, macOS, and Linux are not currently shipping. The download page has the current list: <a href="/download/">/download/</a>.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I install Pulse?',
    a: 'Go to <a href="/download/">/download/</a> and pick your platform. Pulse for Windows is a 12 MB side-panel installer (NSIS or MSI). Pulse for Android is a 1.32 MB APK. Both are signed binaries with SHA-256 checksums published on the download page. No account, no email, no activation server roundtrip.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do updates work?',
    a: 'Pulse checks for updates against a public manifest on this site. If a newer version is available, the app shows an in-app banner with a one-click download. Updates are not silent and not forced. You can disable update checks in settings.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I report a bug or suggest a feature?',
    a: 'Open an issue on the public GitHub repository. The repo lives under the same organization that hosts this site. Bug reports, feature requests, and pull requests are all welcome. There is no support email, no Discord, and no private ticket queue for general questions.',
  },
];

// FAQPage JSON-LD for the structured-data block.
const faqJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ''),
    },
  })),
};
---

<Base
  title={PAGE_TITLE}
  description={PAGE_DESC}
  ogImage="/og-home.png"
  ctaText="Start free ↓"
  ctaHref="/download/"
  ctaVisible={true}
  footerLicense=""
  footerVersion=""
>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  
  {/* R251: header is rendered by <Base/> via <RayHeader/> */}


  <main id="main">
    <!-- ─── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="home-hero faq-hero">
      <div class="bg-glow"></div>
      <div class="container home-hero__grid">
        <div class="home-hero__copy reveal">
          <h1 class="home-hero__title">
            Frequently asked<br /><span class="home-hero__hl">questions.</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="home-hero__sub">
            Plain answers about what Pulse is, what it costs, what it does
            with your data, and what it does not. No marketing speak, no
            fine print, no "contact sales".
          </p>
          <p class="home-hero__meta">
            {faqs.length} questions · Free + Pro · last updated 2026-08-18
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── FAQ list ──────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="faq-page" id="questions">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="faq-page__list">
          {faqs.map((f, i) => (
            <details class="faq__item reveal" open={i === 0}>
              <summary class="faq__q">
                <span class="faq__q-text">{f.q}</span>
                <svg class="faq__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                  <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="faq__a" set:html={f.a} />
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>

        <aside class="faq-page__aside reveal">
          <h2>More places to look.</h2>
          <ul role="list">
            <li><a href="/download/">Download Pulse for Windows or Android</a></li>
            <li><a href="/pricing/">Free vs Pro pricing</a></li>
            <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy and data model</a></li>
            <li><a href="/license/">License</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/TimesNuRoman/pulse" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source on GitHub</a></li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer license="" version="" />

  <!-- FAQPage structured data for search engines.
       Mirror of the visible Q&A — generated from the same `faqs` array
       so both stay in sync. -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqJsonLd)} />
</Base>

<style>
  /* ─── FAQ item (matches compare.astro / pricing.astro) ─────
     Same .faq__q / .faq__item / .faq__chev / .faq__a class
     names so the 12-hard-rules min-height check stays happy and
     the page matches the in-site FAQ style. */
  .faq__item {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    transition: border-color var(--dur) var(--ease), background var(--dur) var(--ease);
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
  }
  .faq__item[open] {
    border-color: var(--purple);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(187, 154, 247, 0.2),
                0 6px 24px rgba(187, 154, 247, 0.08);
  }
  .faq__q {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    min-height: 56px;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    user-select: none;
    color: var(--fg);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .faq__q::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq__q::marker { display: none; }
  .faq__q-text { flex: 1; line-height: 1.4; }
  .faq__chev {
    color: var(--muted);
    transition: transform var(--dur) var(--ease), color var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }
  .faq__item[open] .faq__chev { transform: rotate(180deg); color: var(--purple); }
  .faq__a {
    padding: 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .faq__a a { color: var(--cyan); }
  .faq__a a:hover { color: var(--purple); }
  .faq__a code {
    background: var(--surface-2);
    padding: 0.05em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.88em;
    color: var(--cyan);
  }

  /* ─── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .faq-hero {
    padding-top: clamp(112px, 14vw, 160px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 7vw, 80px);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .faq-hero .home-hero__title { max-width: 18ch; }

  /* ─── FAQ list + aside ───────────────────────────── */
  .faq-page {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px) clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px);
  }
  .faq-page .container {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }
  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .faq-page .container {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 280px;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
  .faq-page__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .faq-page__aside {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    position: sticky;
    top: 88px;
  }
  .faq-page__aside h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }
  .faq-page__aside ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .faq-page__aside a {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed transparent;
    transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease), border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }
  .faq-page__aside a:hover {
    color: var(--purple);
    border-bottom-color: var(--purple);
  }
  .nav__link.is-current {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>

